WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
When a blood vessel widens in the body, what made it relax?

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.560
Nerves, hormones, wall stretch, and local chemicals all pull on it at once.

3
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.600
To test one signal cleanly, physiologists take a living piece of tissue out of the

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.600
body.

5
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:23.553
They mount that cut ring of blood vessel inside a glass chamber called an organ

6
00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:27.793
bath. Nerves and circulating hormones are now gone.

7
00:00:29.013 --> 00:00:33.813
The experimenter controls the fluid around the ring, the load stretching it, and

8
00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:35.133
every chemical dripped in.

9
00:00:36.353 --> 00:00:39.553
A trace shows whether the ring pulls tighter or relaxes.

10
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:45.497
Every vessel has a single-cell inner lining called the endothelium, sitting over

11
00:00:45.497 --> 00:00:51.657
smooth muscle. Drip acetylcholine into the bath around an intact ring, and the ring

12
00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:55.957
relaxes. That illustrates the method's guiding idea.

13
00:00:57.317 --> 00:01:01.677
Remove a living tissue to control its bath and test one cause at a time.

14
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.260
Now change just one part in the same bath.

15
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.880
Gently rub off that thin inner lining, leaving the smooth muscle wall behind.

16
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.920
Drip acetylcholine in again.

17
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.640
Predict what happens: does the ring still relax?

18
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.023
No, without its lining, the ring stays tight.

19
00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:30.483
Acetylcholine does not relax smooth muscle directly.

20
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:35.083
It acts on endothelial cells, which make nitric oxide.

21
00:01:36.363 --> 00:01:41.943
Small and uncharged, nitric oxide crosses freely into neighboring smooth muscle and

22
00:01:41.943 --> 00:01:48.403
relaxes it. Comparing intact and rubbed rings exposed the messenger; later work

23
00:01:48.403 --> 00:01:49.843
showed it was nitric oxide.

24
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:53.767
Still, an isolated bath can mislead you.

25
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:59.427
In a frog nerve and muscle, temperature follows surroundings, and cooling slows

26
00:01:59.427 --> 00:02:06.727
conduction. So a room-temperature frog value is not a human value at 37 °C.

27
00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:13.087
Nerve speed is distance over nerve delay, so first subtract junction and muscle

28
00:02:13.087 --> 00:02:19.167
delays. Guard against mistakes with matched controls, subtracted delays, and species

29
00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.167
checks.

30
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.800
With controls like those, isolated preparations unlocked major discoveries.

31
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:33.620
In 1980, Robert Furchgott and John Zawadzki ran that exact organ-bath test on rabbit

32
00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:40.360
aortic rings. Only intact rings relaxed to acetylcholine, showing that the lining

33
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.180
sends a signal to the muscle beneath.

34
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:50.000
In 1970, Kokko held tiny rabbit kidney tubules, thin descending limbs, between glass

35
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.520
pipettes. He flowed controlled fluid through the inside while setting the bath

36
00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:02.500
outside. That isolated perfused tubule showed low sodium permeability and no

37
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.520
detectable active salt transport.

38
00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.880
Water permeability, though, still varies across species.

39
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.863
And Dale and Feldberg solved a speed problem.

40
00:03:14.123 --> 00:03:19.583
An enzyme called acetylcholinesterase clears acetylcholine from the nerve-muscle gap

41
00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:25.823
in milliseconds. They blocked that enzyme and used a living muscle as a detector to

42
00:03:25.823 --> 00:03:31.803
catch it. Strip away competing body signals, keep the tissue alive, and one

43
00:03:31.803 --> 00:03:33.783
controlled test can reveal the cause.
